= Sustainability integration
Operational Technology (OT) environments are used to control and monitor physical processes in many sectors, including industry, energy, and transportation. A failure in these systems can have significant consequences for service availability, production, as well as the safety of facilities and people. It is therefore essential to be able to test their behaviour under controlled conditions in order to identify potential issues before they occur in a real environment.

This thesis focuses on the development of probes for testing OT environments. The objective is to provide a flexible tool capable of verifying the behaviour and robustness of these infrastructures under different conditions. The project therefore aims to facilitate their validation and contribute to improving their reliability and resilience.

In this context, the project can be related to several Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) defined by the United Nations. The most direct connection is with *SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure*, which promotes reliable, sustainable, and resilient infrastructure as well as innovation. Developing a solution that enables OT infrastructures to be tested and validated directly supports this objective. By facilitating distributed and repeatable testing, the developed probes can contribute to improving the reliability of industrial systems and supporting their evolution.

The project can also be linked to *SDG 12 – Responsible Consumption and Production*. The ability to automate and repeat certain testing operations makes it possible to identify problems more quickly after modifications to a system. Better validation of infrastructures can therefore help reduce failures, unnecessary interventions, and the resources required for maintenance.

Finally, the project has an indirect connection with *SDG 8 – Decent Work and Economic Growth*. Automating certain testing operations reduces the amount of manual and repetitive work performed by engineers and operators. This allows them to dedicate more time to analysing results, solving problems, and improving systems.

Overall, the project contributes primarily to SDG 9 by providing an innovative solution for improving the validation and reliability of OT infrastructures. It also indirectly supports SDGs 12 and 8 by promoting more efficient use of resources and reducing repetitive manual testing operations.